Hi there!
Putting the error log was very helpful! Always put it when you encounter an error on your game
Now, as I can see on both plugins, the problem is that NRP plugin puts the Skill Points on the Game_Enemy class, which is used as the default RPG Maker enemy.
But, the VSMA plugin, does not use the Game_Enemy class as the enemy. It uses a new one,
Game_EnemyActor, that inherists from Game_Battler.
As so the function "skillPoint" does not exist on the Game_EnemyActor. Therefore, throws an error.
I just did a quick look, don't know if it will work. I believe you could try one of these approaches and see if it will work.
1 - Faster, but not so sure if it will work. Open the VSMA plugin with any text editor, go to the line 87, or find the line with "class Game_EnemyActor extends Game_Battler{"
Replace Game_Battler with Game_Enemy.
2 - On the VSMA plugin, add the function on the Game_EnemyActor:
JavaScript:
skillPoint() {
    const a = this; // eval参照用

    let skillPoint = 0;

    // 設定値が存在する場合
    const metaSkillPoint = this.enemy().meta.SkillPoint;

    if (metaSkillPoint != undefined) {
        skillPoint = eval(metaSkillPoint);

    // 既定値が存在する場合
    } else if (pDefaultEnemySkillPoint != undefined) {
        skillPoint = eval(pDefaultEnemySkillPoint);
    }

    // rateを乗算する。
    const rate = this.enemy().meta.SkillPointRate;
    if (rate != undefined) {
        skillPoint = Math.round(skillPoint * rate / 100);
    }
    return skillPoint;
}
See if any of them will work. My intention was not to just avoid the crash, but also make them compatible. Although I just did a quick look into it.

