Hi, sorry for late reply. My computer basically killed itself before I had the chance and I've only just got it working again (msi series, cooked motherboard and keyboard).
Anyway, I tried both of those and I got an error code when I tried starting a battle. I've attached the devlogs for both (first for 1, second for 2). It was the 'Cannot read property 'enemy' of undefined' error.
The good news is that I have found a possible workaround.
See, the plugin has a feature where you can increase a actor's Skill Points via an event. So what I've done is on all my troop events, I've created a page for each enemy, which triggers when that enemy's HP hits 0%. The event increases the SP of all party members by 1 (or whatever number I need it to). Three enemies killed, everyone gets 3 SP, one boss killed, everyone gets 10, etc. etc.
It's tedious to do that with all my troops, but so far it seems to be working.
I'm just wondering if it will work with more complex fights and multiple events, or if there's a situation where enemies can revive (although I don't think my game calls for that feature).
It's a possible solution, at least, if the initial problem remains unsolvable.
